{"id":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:homotopy-of-paths","title":"def:homotopy-of-paths","path":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.md","line":28,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.tex#def:homotopy-of-paths","uses":["[[references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter0#def:homotopy]]","[[references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:path]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.tex","label":"def:homotopy-of-paths","line":43,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Homotopy of paths and homotopic paths]\n\\label{def:homotopy-of-paths}\n\n\\uses{def:homotopy, def:path}\n\n\\group{Fundamental Group}\n\nA homotopy of paths in $X$ is a family $f_t:I\\to X$, $0\\leq t\\leq1$, with fixed\nendpoints $f_t(0)=x_0$ and $f_t(1)=x_1$, such that\n$F:I\\times I\\to X$, $F(s,t)=f_t(s)$, is continuous. We write $f_0\\simeq f_1$\nwhen such a homotopy exists.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Homotopy of paths and homotopic paths] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a686f6d6f746f70792d6f662d7061746873\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FHatcher%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter0%23def%3Ahomotopy\">↗ def:homotopy</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FHatcher%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter1%23def%3Apath\">↗ def:path</a> <p></p>\\group Fundamental Group <p></p>A homotopy of paths in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$X$\">$X$</span> is a family <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f_t:I\\to X$\">$f_t:I\\to X$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$0\\leq t\\leq 1$\">$0\\leq t\\leq 1$</span>, with fixed endpoints <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f_t(0)=x_0$\">$f_t(0)=x_0$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f_t(1)=x_1$\">$f_t(1)=x_1$</span>, such that <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F:I\\times I\\to X$\">$F:I\\times I\\to X$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F(s,t)=f_t(s)$\">$F(s,t)=f_t(s)$</span>, is continuous. We write <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f_0\\simeq f_1$\">$f_0\\simeq f_1$</span> when such a homotopy exists. ","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: group"]},"previous":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:path","next":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#ex:linear-homotopies-convex","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter0#def:homotopy","title":"def:homotopy","label":"def:homotopy"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:path","title":"def:path","label":"def:path"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#ex:linear-homotopies-convex","title":"ex:linear-homotopies-convex","label":"ex:linear-homotopies-convex"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#prop:homotopy-paths-equivalence-relation","title":"prop:homotopy-paths-equivalence-relation","label":"prop:homotopy-paths-equivalence-relation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:loop-and-pi1-set","title":"def:loop-and-pi1-set","label":"def:loop-and-pi1-set"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#prop:simply-connected-iff-unique-path-class","title":"prop:simply-connected-iff-unique-path-class","label":"prop:simply-connected-iff-unique-path-class"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:homotopy-of-paths","title":"def:homotopy-of-paths","tex":"\\begin{definition}[Homotopy of paths and homotopic paths]\n\\label{def:homotopy-of-paths}\n\n\\uses{def:homotopy, def:path}\n\n\\group{Fundamental Group}\n\nA homotopy of paths in $X$ is a family $f_t:I\\to X$, $0\\leq t\\leq1$, with fixed\nendpoints $f_t(0)=x_0$ and $f_t(1)=x_1$, such that\n$F:I\\times I\\to X$, $F(s,t)=f_t(s)$, is continuous. We write $f_0\\simeq f_1$\nwhen such a homotopy exists.\n\\end{definition}","source":"tex/references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter0#def:homotopy","title":"def:homotopy","description":""},{"node":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:path","title":"def:path","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}